  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "autoloader-generic",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "The app ships no composer/autoload.php, so the server registers its generic loader for lib/ and looks every class up in the file system.",
        "  A composer/composer.json with config.vendor-dir \".\", config.optimize-autoloader true, a config.autoloader-suffix and autoload.psr-4 {\"OCA\\\\LoginNotes\\\\\": \"../lib/\"} makes composer dump-autoload write composer/autoload.php with a class map; the code of the app does not change."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vendor-shadows-server",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "psr/event-dispatcher 1.0.0, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 33 to 35",
        "symfony/deprecation-contracts v3.7.1, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 33 to 35"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "vendor/ ships 2 packages that the server ships itself in a major of Nextcloud 33 to 35. Both copies define the same classes, and the autoloader that is asked first decides which version runs.",
